#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:94
msgid ""
"``Failed to get the shape``: building it produced nothing. The reason is in "
"the log above the verdict - the error the script raised, the file that could"
" not be read or fetched, the link of an assembly that names an object nobody"
" declares. Build it on its own to see it again: ``pc --no-ansi info "
"<object>`` or ``pc --no-ansi render -t png <object>``."
msgstr ""
"``Failed to get the shape``: construirlo no produjo nada. El motivo está en "
"el registro, encima del veredicto - el error que lanzó el script, el archivo"
" que no se pudo leer ni descargar, el enlace de un ensamblaje que nombra un "
"objeto que nadie declara. Constrúyalo por separado para volver a verlo: ``pc"
" --no-ansi info <object>`` o ``pc --no-ansi render -t png <object>``."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:95
msgid ""
"A verdict remembered from an earlier run is said again with \"remembered "
"from an earlier run\": once the cause is fixed, ``pc --cache-bypass test`` "
"asks again rather than reading the cache."
msgstr ""
"Un veredicto recordado de una ejecución anterior se vuelve a dar con "
"\"recordado de una ejecución anterior\": una vez corregida la causa, ``pc "
"--cache-bypass test`` pregunta de nuevo en lugar de leer la caché."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:100
msgid "``manufacturability``: Can be made or bought"
msgstr "``manufacturability``: Se puede fabricar o comprar"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:102
msgid ""
"**Applies to** every object that does not say ``manufacturable: false``. "
"``pc test -f manufacturability <object>`` runs it alone."
msgstr ""
"**Se aplica a** todos los objetos que no digan ``manufacturable: false``. "
"``pc test -f manufacturability <object>`` la ejecuta sola."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:104
msgid ""
"Whether the object can be had: bought from somebody who sells it, or made by"
" a method it declares. It asks for exactly what ``pc supply`` would order "
"and what ``pc instructions`` would tell somebody to do."
msgstr ""
"Si el objeto se puede conseguir: comprado a alguien que lo vende, o "
"fabricado por un método que declara. Pregunta exactamente por lo que ``pc "
"supply`` pediría y por lo que ``pc instructions`` le diría a alguien que "
"hiciera."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:106
msgid ""
"Every object has to be reproducible: one read from a file the package "
"fetches (``fileFrom:``) has to pin the file with ``fileHash:``, or name a "
"vendor and SKU to order it by, so that it is known which bytes it is made "
"from."
msgstr ""
"Todos los objetos tienen que ser reproducibles: uno que se lee de un archivo"
" que el paquete descarga (``fileFrom:``) tiene que fijar el archivo con "
"``fileHash:``, o nombrar un fabricante y un SKU con los que pedirlo, de modo"
" que se sepa de qué bytes está hecho."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:107
msgid ""
"A part is bought (``vendor:`` and ``sku:``, and a supplier that carries it) "
"or made (``manufacturing:`` with a ``method:``). A part that is made needs a"
" manufacturing tolerance, and the stock it is made from (``manufacturing: "
"source:``) has to pass these checks itself. The ``software:`` it declares "
"has to resolve, to the file that was meant."
msgstr ""
"Una pieza se compra (``vendor:`` y ``sku:``, y un proveedor que la "
"distribuya) o se fabrica (``manufacturing:`` con un ``method:``). Una pieza "
"que se fabrica necesita una tolerancia de fabricación, y el material del que"
" se fabrica (``manufacturing: source:``) tiene que pasar él mismo estas "
"comprobaciones. El ``software:`` que declara tiene que resolverse, al "
"archivo que se pretendía."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:108
msgid ""
"An assembly is either sold assembled (bought, and nothing inside it is "
"looked at), or assembled: then every step has to be one somebody can follow "
"- each item after the first says what it is joined to and how - and "
"everything it is procured from has to pass these checks on its own."
msgstr ""
"Un ensamblaje se vende ya montado (comprado, y no se mira nada de su "
"interior) o se monta: entonces cada paso tiene que ser uno que alguien pueda"
" seguir - cada elemento después del primero dice a qué se une y cómo - y "
"todo aquello de lo que se abastece tiene que pasar estas comprobaciones por "
"su cuenta."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:113
msgid ""
"An object that says ``manufacturable: false`` - a model of something "
"somebody else makes, an import kept as it arrived, a scene (which is not "
"manufacturable unless it says so). A sketch is checked for being "
"reproducible and for nothing else."
msgstr ""
"Un objeto que dice ``manufacturable: false`` - un modelo de algo que fabrica"
" otra persona, una importación conservada tal como llegó, una escena (que no"
" es fabricable a menos que lo diga). De un boceto se comprueba que sea "
"reproducible y nada más."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:118
msgid ""
"``It is not reproducible: ...``: pin the file with ``fileHash:`` (``pc add``"
" writes one for an object it adds from a URL), carry the file in the "
"package, or name a ``vendor:`` and ``sku:``."
msgstr ""
"``It is not reproducible: ...``: fije el archivo con ``fileHash:`` (``pc "
"add`` escribe uno para un objeto que añade desde una URL), lleve el archivo "
"en el paquete, o nombre un ``vendor:`` y un ``sku:``."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:119
msgid ""
"``Cannot be purchased or manufactured``: add a ``manufacturing:`` section "
"with a ``method:`` (see the ``manufacturability-*`` checks for each method),"
" or a ``vendor:`` and ``sku:`` - or say ``manufacturable: false`` if nobody "
"is going to make it."
msgstr ""
"``Cannot be purchased or manufactured``: añada una sección "
"``manufacturing:`` con un ``method:`` (véanse las comprobaciones "
"``manufacturability-*`` para cada método), o un ``vendor:`` y un ``sku:`` - "
"o diga ``manufacturable: false`` si nadie va a fabricarlo."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:120
msgid ""
"``No suppliers found`` / ``No suppliers provide the part``: name a supplier "
"that carries it, or make it instead."
msgstr ""
"``No suppliers found`` / ``No suppliers provide the part``: nombre un "
"proveedor que la distribuya, o fabríquela en su lugar."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:121
msgid ""
"``No manufacturing tolerance is specified``: give the part a ``tolerance``, "
"which a part that is made needs to be made to anything."
msgstr ""
"``No manufacturing tolerance is specified``: dé a la pieza una "
"``tolerance``, que una pieza que se fabrica necesita para poder fabricarse "
"en absoluto."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:122
msgid ""
"``The stock '...' it is made from is not found`` / ``cannot be had``: fix "
"the name under ``manufacturing: source:``, or make the stock obtainable."
msgstr ""
"``The stock '...' it is made from is not found`` / ``cannot be had``: "
"corrija el nombre bajo ``manufacturing: source:``, o haga que el material se"
" pueda conseguir."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:123
msgid ""
"``Step '...' can't be followed: ...``: give that link a ``connect:`` and say"
" how it goes on - a ``how:``, or a mating or an interface that says it."
msgstr ""
"``Step '...' can't be followed: ...``: dé a ese enlace un ``connect:`` y "
"diga cómo se monta - un ``how:``, o un emparejamiento o una interfaz que lo "
"diga."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:124
msgid ""
"``Missing part or assembly '...' is referenced`` / ``Non-manufacturable ... "
"is referenced``: what the assembly is made of has to exist and be "
"manufacturable."
msgstr ""
"``Missing part or assembly '...' is referenced`` / ``Non-manufacturable ... "
"is referenced``: aquello de lo que está hecho el ensamblaje tiene que "
"existir y ser fabricable."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:127
#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:237
#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:263
#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:288
#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:339
#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:470
#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:521
#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:549
#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:577
#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:605
#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:633
msgid "Settings"
msgstr "Ajustes"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:129
msgid ""
"``manufacturable:`` on the object or its package; ``vendor:``, ``sku:``, "
"``fileFrom:``, ``fileHash:``, ``software:``, ``manufacturing:`` and the "
"part's ``tolerance``."
msgstr ""
"``manufacturable:`` en el objeto o en su paquete; ``vendor:``, ``sku:``, "
"``fileFrom:``, ``fileHash:``, ``software:``, ``manufacturing:`` y la "
"``tolerance`` de la pieza."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:134
msgid "``manufacturability-additive``: Additive: a closed solid"
msgstr "``manufacturability-additive``: Aditivo: un sólido cerrado"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:136
msgid ""
"**Applies to** a part with ``manufacturing: method: additive``. ``pc test -f"
" manufacturability-additive <object>`` runs it alone."
msgstr ""
"**Se aplica a** una pieza con ``manufacturing: method: additive``. ``pc test"
" -f manufacturability-additive <object>`` la ejecuta sola."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:138
msgid ""
"Whether a part to be printed is a closed solid: a body with no open edges, "
"which is what a slicer needs to know what is inside it."
msgstr ""
"Si una pieza que se va a imprimir es un sólido cerrado: un cuerpo sin "
"aristas abiertas, que es lo que un laminador necesita para saber qué hay "
"dentro de él."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:143
#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:163
#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:186
#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:206
msgid "Anything but a part, and a part made by any other method."
msgstr ""
"Cualquier cosa que no sea una pieza, y una pieza fabricada por cualquier "
"otro método."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:148
msgid ""
"``The shape is not solid``: the part has open edges - faces that do not "
"meet. Close the model in the tool it comes from, or export it as a solid "
"rather than as a surface."
msgstr ""
"``The shape is not solid``: la pieza tiene aristas abiertas - caras que no "
"se encuentran. Cierre el modelo en la herramienta de la que viene, o "
"expórtelo como sólido en lugar de como superficie."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:149
#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:192
msgid "``Failed to get the shape``: it did not build; see ``cad``."
msgstr "``Failed to get the shape``: no se construyó; véase ``cad``."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:154
msgid "``manufacturability-subtractive``: Subtractive: cut from its stock"
msgstr ""
"``manufacturability-subtractive``: Sustractivo: cortado de su material de "
"partida"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:156
msgid ""
"**Applies to** a part with ``manufacturing: method: subtractive``. ``pc test"
" -f manufacturability-subtractive <object>`` runs it alone."
msgstr ""
"**Se aplica a** una pieza con ``manufacturing: method: subtractive``. ``pc "
"test -f manufacturability-subtractive <object>`` la ejecuta sola."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:158
msgid ""
"Whether a part to be cut out of stock can be: the stock is named, the "
"machine sections can be read, the part is a closed solid, and it lies inside"
" its stock with material to take away. Cutting removes material and never "
"adds it, so a part that sticks out of its stock cannot be cut from it."
msgstr ""
"Si una pieza que se va a cortar de un material de partida puede cortarse: el"
" material de partida está nombrado, las secciones de máquina se pueden leer,"
" la pieza es un sólido cerrado, y queda dentro de su material de partida con"
" material que quitar. Cortar quita material y nunca lo añade, así que una "
"pieza que sobresale de su material de partida no se puede cortar de él."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:168
msgid ""
"``The subtractive declaration states no 'source'``: name the stock the part "
"is cut from under ``manufacturing: source:``."
msgstr ""
"``The subtractive declaration states no 'source'``: nombre bajo "
"``manufacturing: source:`` el material de partida del que se corta la pieza."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:169
msgid ""
"``The subtractive declaration says ...``: a ``cnc:``, ``laser:``, ``drill:``"
" or ``cut:`` section has a key it does not take, or a value it cannot read; "
"the sentence names it."
msgstr ""
"``The subtractive declaration says ...``: una sección ``cnc:``, ``laser:``, "
"``drill:`` o ``cut:`` tiene una clave que no acepta, o un valor que no puede"
" leer; la frase lo nombra."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:170
msgid ""
"``It does not fit the stock '...': ... mm3 of it is outside``: make the "
"stock larger, or place it so that it encloses the part."
msgstr ""
"``It does not fit the stock '...': ... mm3 of it is outside``: agrande el "
"material de partida, o colóquelo de modo que encierre la pieza."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:171
msgid ""
"``The stock '...' is the same solid as the part, so nothing is cut from "
"it``: ``source:`` names the part itself, or a copy of it; name the blank "
"instead."
msgstr ""
"``The stock '...' is the same solid as the part, so nothing is cut from "
"it``: ``source:`` nombra la pieza misma, o una copia de ella; nombre en su "
"lugar la pieza en bruto."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:172
msgid ""
"``The shape is not solid``: close the model, as for ``manufacturability-"
"additive``."
msgstr ""
"``The shape is not solid``: cierre el modelo, como en ``manufacturability-"
"additive``."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:177
msgid "``manufacturability-forming``: Forming: a closed solid"
msgstr "``manufacturability-forming``: Conformado: un sólido cerrado"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:179
msgid ""
"**Applies to** a part with ``manufacturing: method: forming``. ``pc test -f "
"manufacturability-forming <object>`` runs it alone."
msgstr ""
"**Se aplica a** una pieza con ``manufacturing: method: forming``. ``pc test "
"-f manufacturability-forming <object>`` la ejecuta sola."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:181
msgid ""
"Whether a part to be formed - moulded, cast, pressed - is a closed solid."
msgstr ""
"Si una pieza que se va a conformar - moldear, fundir, prensar - es un sólido"
" cerrado."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:191
msgid "``The shape is not solid``: the part has open edges; close the model."
msgstr ""
"``The shape is not solid``: la pieza tiene aristas abiertas; cierre el "
"modelo."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:197
msgid "``manufacturability-sheet-metal``: Sheet metal: a flat blank and bends"
msgstr ""
"``manufacturability-sheet-metal``: Chapa metálica: una pieza en bruto plana "
"y pliegues"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:199
msgid ""
"**Applies to** a part with ``manufacturing: method: sheet_metal``. ``pc test"
" -f manufacturability-sheet-metal <object>`` runs it alone."
msgstr ""
"**Se aplica a** una pieza con ``manufacturing: method: sheet_metal``. ``pc "
"test -f manufacturability-sheet-metal <object>`` la ejecuta sola."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:201
msgid ""
"Whether a sheet metal part can be bent out of what it names: a blank that is"
" flat on both faces (``source:``), and a sketch of the bend lines "
"(``instructions:``) in which every line says its angle, its inner radius and"
" which way it goes. Both questions are asked every time, so one run says "
"everything that is wrong."
msgstr ""
"Si una pieza de chapa metálica se puede plegar a partir de lo que nombra: "
"una pieza en bruto plana por ambas caras (``source:``), y un boceto de las "
"líneas de plegado (``instructions:``) en el que cada línea dice su ángulo, "
"su radio interior y hacia qué lado va. Las dos preguntas se plantean "
"siempre, así que una sola ejecución dice todo lo que está mal."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:211
msgid ""
"``The sheet metal declaration states no 'source'`` (or ``'instructions'``): "
"name the flat blank and the sketch of the bend lines."
msgstr ""
"``The sheet metal declaration states no 'source'`` (o ``'instructions'``): "
"nombre la pieza en bruto plana y el boceto de las líneas de plegado."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:212
msgid ""
"``... is not flat on the bottom`` (or ``top``): ``source:`` has to be the "
"flat blank, not the bent part."
msgstr ""
"``... is not flat on the bottom`` (o ``top``): ``source:`` tiene que ser la "
"pieza en bruto plana, no la pieza plegada."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:213
msgid ""
"``... draws no bend lines``: the sketch has to draw each bend as a line; a "
"layer can be picked with parameters (``bends;include=BEND_UP,BEND_DOWN``)."
msgstr ""
"``... draws no bend lines``: el boceto tiene que dibujar cada pliegue como "
"una línea; se puede elegir una capa con parámetros "
"(``bends;include=BEND_UP,BEND_DOWN``)."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:214
msgid ""
"``The bend drawn by the ... cannot be made: ...``: annotate the line with an"
" ``angle`` above 0 and below 360 degrees, a ``radius`` above 0 (a bend, not "
"a fold), and a ``direction`` of ``up`` or ``down``."
msgstr ""
"``The bend drawn by the ... cannot be made: ...``: anote la línea con un "
"``angle`` mayor que 0 y menor que 360 grados, un ``radius`` mayor que 0 (un "
"pliegue, no un doblez a tope), y una ``direction`` de ``up`` o ``down``."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:219
msgid "``manufacturability-laser``: Laser: faces along or across the beam"
msgstr ""
"``manufacturability-laser``: Láser: caras a lo largo del haz o transversales"
" a él"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:221
msgid ""
"**Applies to** a part made by ``method: subtractive`` that names a "
"``laser:`` machine. ``pc test -f manufacturability-laser <object>`` runs it "
"alone."
msgstr ""
"**Se aplica a** una pieza fabricada por ``method: subtractive`` que nombra "
"una máquina ``laser:``. ``pc test -f manufacturability-laser <object>`` la "
"ejecuta sola."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:223
msgid ""
"Whether a laser cutting along the tool axis can make the part: every face "
"has to be either a wall along the axis or a face across it, and there has to"
" be a wall to cut. A laser cuts straight through, so a chamfer, a taper or a"
" fillet that is neither is not something it can make. Thickness, material "
"and power are not checked."
msgstr ""
"Si un láser que corta a lo largo del eje de la herramienta puede fabricar la"
" pieza: cada cara tiene que ser o una pared a lo largo del eje o una cara "
"transversal a él, y tiene que haber una pared que cortar. Un láser corta en "
"línea recta, así que un chaflán, un cono o un redondeo que no sea ninguna de"
" las dos cosas no es algo que pueda fabricar. El espesor, el material y la "
"potencia no se comprueban."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:228
msgid ""
"Anything but a part, a part made by another method, and a subtractive part "
"that names no ``laser:`` machine - a part that names no machine at all is "
"taken to be milled."
msgstr ""
"Cualquier cosa que no sea una pieza, una pieza fabricada por otro método, y "
"una pieza sustractiva que no nombra ninguna máquina ``laser:`` - una pieza "
"que no nombra ninguna máquina se toma por fresada."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:233
msgid ""
"``A laser cutting along ... cannot make it: N of its faces are neither along"
" ... nor across it``: remove the faces at an angle (the worst is named), or "
"set ``toolAxis:`` to the direction the beam really goes."
msgstr ""
"``A laser cutting along ... cannot make it: N of its faces are neither along"
" ... nor across it``: quite las caras inclinadas (se nombra la peor), o "
"ponga ``toolAxis:`` en la dirección en la que realmente va el haz."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:234
msgid ""
"``It has no wall along ... for a laser to cut``: the axis is wrong, or the "
"part is not something a laser makes."
msgstr ""
"``It has no wall along ... for a laser to cut``: el eje está mal, o la pieza"
" no es algo que fabrique un láser."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:239
msgid ""
"``manufacturing: laser:`` - ``toolAxis:`` (or ``along:``, default ``-Z``) "
"and the job keys (``kerf``, ``power``, ``feed``, ``direction``, "
"``implementation``)."
msgstr ""
"``manufacturing: laser:`` - ``toolAxis:`` (o ``along:``, ``-Z`` por defecto)"
" y las claves del trabajo (``kerf``, ``power``, ``feed``, ``direction``, "
"``implementation``)."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:244
msgid "``manufacturability-drill``: Drill: round holes along the axis"
msgstr ""
"``manufacturability-drill``: Taladrado: agujeros redondos a lo largo del eje"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:246
msgid ""
"**Applies to** a part made by ``method: subtractive`` that names a "
"``drill:`` machine. ``pc test -f manufacturability-drill <object>`` runs it "
"alone."
msgstr ""
"**Se aplica a** una pieza fabricada por ``method: subtractive`` que nombra "
"una máquina ``drill:``. ``pc test -f manufacturability-drill <object>`` la "
"ejecuta sola."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:248
msgid ""
"Whether a drill working along the tool axis can make what is taken away: "
"every wall has to be along the axis and round. Measured on the material "
"removed from the stock when ``source:`` names one, and on the part itself "
"otherwise."
msgstr ""
"Si un taladro que trabaja a lo largo del eje de la herramienta puede hacer "
"lo que se quita: cada pared tiene que estar a lo largo del eje y ser "
"redonda. Se mide sobre el material retirado del material de partida cuando "
"``source:`` nombra uno, y sobre la pieza misma en caso contrario."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:253
msgid ""
"Anything but a part, a part made by another method, and a subtractive part "
"that names no ``drill:`` machine."
msgstr ""
"Cualquier cosa que no sea una pieza, una pieza fabricada por otro método, y "
"una pieza sustractiva que no nombra ninguna máquina ``drill:``."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:258
msgid ""
"``There is no hole along ... for a drill to make``: the axis is wrong, or "
"there is nothing to drill."
msgstr ""
"``There is no hole along ... for a drill to make``: el eje está mal, o no "
"hay nada que taladrar."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:259
msgid ""
"``A drill only makes round holes, and N of the M walls along ... are not "
"round``: make the holes round, or cut the other shapes another way. When the"
" stock is not named, the part's own outline counts as drilled: name it with "
"``source:``."
msgstr ""
"``A drill only makes round holes, and N of the M walls along ... are not "
"round``: haga los agujeros redondos, o corte las otras formas de otra "
"manera. Cuando no se nombra el material de partida, el propio contorno de la"
" pieza cuenta como taladrado: nómbrelo con ``source:``."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:260
msgid ""
"``A drill working along ... cannot make it``: some walls are not along the "
"axis; check ``toolAxis:``."
msgstr ""
"``A drill working along ... cannot make it``: algunas paredes no están a lo "
"largo del eje; compruebe ``toolAxis:``."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:265
msgid ""
"``manufacturing: drill:`` - ``toolAxis:`` (or ``along:``), and the job keys "
"(``diameter``, ``peck``, ``plunge``, ``speed``, ``safe_z``); "
"``manufacturing: source:``."
msgstr ""
"``manufacturing: drill:`` - ``toolAxis:`` (o ``along:``), y las claves del "
"trabajo (``diameter``, ``peck``, ``plunge``, ``speed``, ``safe_z``); "
"``manufacturing: source:``."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:270
msgid "``manufacturability-cut``: Cut: the cuts make the part"
msgstr "``manufacturability-cut``: Corte: los cortes dan la pieza"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:272
msgid ""
"**Applies to** a part made by ``method: subtractive`` that names a ``cut:`` "
"machine. ``pc test -f manufacturability-cut <object>`` runs it alone."
msgstr ""
"**Se aplica a** una pieza fabricada por ``method: subtractive`` que nombra "
"una máquina ``cut:``. ``pc test -f manufacturability-cut <object>`` la "
"ejecuta sola."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:274
msgid ""
"Whether cutting the stock where the part says gives the part: each declared "
"cut is a plane, the stock is cut at every one, and what is left has to be "
"the part. No cut may take nothing off."
msgstr ""
"Si cortar el material de partida donde dice la pieza da la pieza: cada corte"
" declarado es un plano, el material de partida se corta en todos ellos, y lo"
" que queda tiene que ser la pieza. Ningún corte puede no quitar nada."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:279
msgid ""
"Anything but a part, a part made by another method, and a subtractive part "
"that names no ``cut:`` machine. A part that names no stock passes here, "
"since ``manufacturability-subtractive`` already says so."
msgstr ""
"Cualquier cosa que no sea una pieza, una pieza fabricada por otro método, y "
"una pieza sustractiva que no nombra ninguna máquina ``cut:``. Una pieza que "
"no nombra ningún material de partida pasa aquí, ya que ``manufacturability-"
"subtractive`` ya lo dice."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:284
msgid ""
"``Cut #N (...) takes nothing off the stock``: the length is longer than the "
"stock, or the axis points away from it."
msgstr ""
"``Cut #N (...) takes nothing off the stock``: la longitud es mayor que el "
"material de partida, o el eje apunta hacia fuera de él."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:285
msgid ""
"``Cutting the stock '...' at ... does not make it: ...``: the cuts leave too"
" much or too little; correct the lengths or the axes."
msgstr ""
"``Cutting the stock '...' at ... does not make it: ...``: los cortes dejan "
"demasiado o demasiado poco; corrija las longitudes o los ejes."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:290
msgid ""
"``manufacturing: cut:`` - ``toolAxis:`` (or ``along:``) and ``cuts:``, each "
"a ``length`` and an optional axis of its own."
msgstr ""
"``manufacturing: cut:`` - ``toolAxis:`` (o ``along:``) y ``cuts:``, cada uno"
" con una ``length`` y, opcionalmente, un eje propio."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:295
msgid "``connect``: Connection instructions"
msgstr "``connect``: Instrucciones de conexión"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:297
msgid ""
"**Applies to** assemblies and scenes. ``pc test -f connect <object>`` runs "
"it alone."
msgstr ""
"**Se aplica a** ensamblajes y escenas. ``pc test -f connect <object>`` la "
"ejecuta sola."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:299
msgid ""
"Whether the assembly's connection instructions can be followed as written: "
"whether anything had to be bent to put it together - a ``how:`` whose "
"minimum is above its maximum, two interfaces that disagree about the thread "
"they share and neither cuts its own, a motion or a physics the joined ends "
"contradict, a joint named twice, a chain that closes on itself. An assembly "
"that says nothing about how its items go on has nothing to contradict, and "
"passes."
msgstr ""
"Si las instrucciones de conexión del ensamblaje se pueden seguir tal como "
"están escritas: si hubo que forzar algo para montarlo - un ``how:`` cuyo "
"mínimo está por encima de su máximo, dos interfaces que no coinciden sobre "
"la rosca que comparten y ninguna de las dos corta la suya, un movimiento o "
"una física que los extremos unidos contradicen, una articulación nombrada "
"dos veces, una cadena que se cierra sobre sí misma. Un ensamblaje que no "
"dice nada sobre cómo se montan sus elementos no tiene nada que contradecir, "
"y pasa."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:304
#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:329
#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:459
msgid "Anything but an assembly or a scene."
msgstr "Cualquier cosa que no sea un ensamblaje o una escena."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:309
msgid ""
"Each failure is ``<link>: <what had to be repaired>``. Fix the declaration "
"it names: the ``how:`` of that link, the interfaces or the mating it joins, "
"or the joint. The list of what is reported is in \"Testing the "
"instructions\" of the assembly documentation."
msgstr ""
"Cada fallo es ``<link>: <what had to be repaired>``. Corrija la declaración "
"que nombra: el ``how:`` de ese enlace, las interfaces o el emparejamiento "
"que une, o la articulación. La lista de lo que se informa está en \"Probar "
"las instrucciones\" de la documentación de ensamblajes."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:314
msgid "``connectivity``: Everything is held in place"
msgstr "``connectivity``: Todo está sujeto en su sitio"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:316
msgid ""
"**Applies to** assemblies and scenes. ``pc test -f connectivity <object>`` "
"runs it alone."
msgstr ""
"**Se aplica a** ensamblajes y escenas. ``pc test -f connectivity <object>`` "
"la ejecuta sola."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:318
msgid ""
"Whether everything an assembly places is placed once, on a port that takes "
"it, and held there. Three mistakes that render perfectly:"
msgstr ""
"Si todo lo que coloca un ensamblaje se coloca una sola vez, en un puerto que"
" lo acepta, y queda sujeto ahí. Tres errores que se renderizan "
"perfectamente:"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:320
msgid "the same part twice in the same place;"
msgstr "la misma pieza dos veces en el mismo sitio;"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:321
msgid ""
"two items connected to one port, when its interface does not say "
"``multiConnect: true``;"
msgstr ""
"dos elementos conectados a un mismo puerto, cuando su interfaz no dice "
"``multiConnect: true``;"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:322
msgid ""
"an item placed by coordinates (``location:``) among items that connect, "
"which says where it ends up but not what holds it there."
msgstr ""
"un elemento colocado por coordenadas (``location:``) entre elementos que se "
"conectan, lo que dice dónde acaba pero no qué lo sujeta ahí."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:324
msgid ""
"An assembly that is to be made (``manufacturable``) is held to more: no item"
" may be placed by coordinates, and every item after the first has to connect"
" to something."
msgstr ""
"A un ensamblaje que se va a fabricar (``manufacturable``) se le exige más: "
"ningún elemento puede colocarse por coordenadas, y todos los elementos "
"después del primero tienen que conectarse con algo."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:334
msgid ""
"``'a' and 'b' are the same part in the same place``: remove one, or move it."
msgstr ""
"``'a' and 'b' are the same part in the same place``: quite uno, o muévalo."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:335
msgid ""
"``'a' and 'b' are both connected to '...' of '...'``: connect one of them "
"elsewhere, or say ``multiConnect: true`` on the interface if the port does "
"take several."
msgstr ""
"``'a' and 'b' are both connected to '...' of '...'``: conecte uno de ellos "
"en otro sitio, o diga ``multiConnect: true`` en la interfaz si el puerto "
"admite varios."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:336
msgid ""
"``'...' is placed by coordinates ...``: replace its ``location:`` with a "
"``connect:`` to what holds it."
msgstr ""
"``'...' is placed by coordinates ...``: sustituya su ``location:`` por un "
"``connect:`` a lo que lo sujeta."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:341
msgid ""
"On the assembly: ``connectivity: allowDuplicates: true`` to allow the same "
"part twice in one place, and ``connectivity: requireAnchored: false`` to "
"allow items placed by coordinates."
msgstr ""
"En el ensamblaje: ``connectivity: allowDuplicates: true`` para permitir la "
"misma pieza dos veces en un mismo sitio, y ``connectivity: requireAnchored: "
"false`` para permitir elementos colocados por coordenadas."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:346
msgid "``requirements``: Meets its requirements"
msgstr "``requirements``: Cumple sus requisitos"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:348
msgid ""
"**Applies to** objects whose ``requirements:`` require ports, interfaces or "
"physical properties. ``pc test -f requirements <object>`` runs it alone."
msgstr ""
"**Se aplica a** los objetos cuyos ``requirements:`` exigen puertos, "
"interfaces o propiedades físicas. ``pc test -f requirements <object>`` la "
"ejecuta sola."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:350
msgid ""
"Whether the model is what its ``requirements:`` say it has to be, as far as "
"that can be measured: each required port is there, facing where it has to; "
"each required interface is implemented, its instances where they have to be;"
" and each required physical property - its mass, its centre of mass, its "
"inertia, its friction - has a value that meets the requirement. Asked again "
"every time, never read from the cache."
msgstr ""
"Si el modelo es lo que sus ``requirements:`` dicen que tiene que ser, en la "
"medida en que eso se pueda medir: cada puerto exigido está ahí, mirando a "
"donde tiene que mirar; cada interfaz exigida está implementada, con sus "
"instancias donde tienen que estar; y cada propiedad física exigida - su "
"masa, su centro de masas, su inercia, su fricción - tiene un valor que "
"cumple el requisito. Se pregunta de nuevo cada vez, nunca se lee de la "
"caché."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:352
msgid ""
"The ``features:`` are sentences rather than measurements, and are judged by "
"the ``/pc:validate`` agent skill. What this check asks of them is only that "
"a ``simulate:`` entry or an analysis scenario naming one (``feature:``) "
"names one that is declared."
msgstr ""
"Las ``features:`` son frases y no mediciones, y las juzga la skill de agente"
" ``/pc:validate``. Lo único que esta comprobación les pide es que una "
"entrada ``simulate:`` o un escenario de análisis que nombre una "
"(``feature:``) nombre una que esté declarada."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:357
msgid ""
"An object that requires no port, interface or physical property, and whose "
"simulations and analysis scenarios name no feature."
msgstr ""
"Un objeto que no exige ningún puerto, interfaz ni propiedad física, y cuyas "
"simulaciones y escenarios de análisis no nombran ninguna característica."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:362
msgid ""
"Each failure is ``<section>: <name>: <required>: <found>`` - what was asked "
"for and what is there instead."
msgstr ""
"Cada fallo es ``<section>: <name>: <required>: <found>`` - qué se pedía y "
"qué hay en su lugar."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:364
msgid ""
"A port or an interface instance that is missing, or faces the wrong way: "
"move it in the model, or correct the requirement if the requirement is what "
"is wrong."
msgstr ""
"Un puerto o una instancia de interfaz que falta, o que mira en la dirección "
"equivocada: muévalo en el modelo, o corrija el requisito si lo que está mal "
"es el requisito."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:365
msgid ""
"``not known: ...``: PartCAD could not find out the value - a mass with no "
"density to work it out from. State the value in a ``physics:`` section, or "
"give the part a ``material:`` with a density. \"Not known\" is not \"met\"."
msgstr ""
"``not known: ...``: PartCAD no pudo averiguar el valor - una masa sin "
"ninguna densidad con la que calcularla. Declare el valor en una sección "
"``physics:``, o dé a la pieza un ``material:`` con densidad. \"No conocido\""
" no es \"cumplido\"."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:366
msgid ""
"``unreadable``: the requirement itself cannot be read; the detail says why."
msgstr ""
"``unreadable``: el requisito mismo no se puede leer; el detalle dice por "
"qué."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:371
msgid "``degenerate``: Has size in every direction"
msgstr "``degenerate``: Tiene tamaño en todas las direcciones"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:373
msgid ""
"**Applies to** parts. ``pc test -f degenerate <object>`` runs it alone."
msgstr ""
"**Se aplica a** las piezas. ``pc test -f degenerate <object>`` la ejecuta "
"sola."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:375
msgid ""
"Whether a part has size in every direction. A part that built as a flat disc"
" or an empty box - a brick whose subfile could not be fetched, a script that"
" returned the wrong thing - renders, exports and measures, and is not the "
"part that was meant. Read from the box measured when the part was built, so "
"it costs next to nothing."
msgstr ""
"Si una pieza tiene tamaño en todas las direcciones. Una pieza que se "
"construyó como un disco plano o una caja vacía - un ladrillo cuyo subarchivo"
" no se pudo descargar, un script que devolvió lo que no debía - se "
"renderiza, se exporta y se mide, y no es la pieza que se pretendía. Se lee "
"de la caja medida cuando se construyó la pieza, así que no cuesta casi nada."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:380
msgid ""
"A sketch, which is flat by definition, and an assembly or a scene, which is "
"checked through its parts."
msgstr ""
"Un boceto, que es plano por definición, y un ensamblaje o una escena, que se"
" comprueban a través de sus piezas."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:385
msgid ""
"``The shape built but occupies no space at all``: nothing came out of the "
"build but an empty shape; find the geometry that went missing."
msgstr ""
"``The shape built but occupies no space at all``: de la construcción no "
"salió más que una forma vacía; busque la geometría que falta."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:386
msgid ""
"``The shape is flat in ...``: it is less than a thousandth of a millimetre "
"thick in one direction - a missing extrusion, a missing file, a surface "
"where a solid was meant."
msgstr ""
"``The shape is flat in ...``: tiene menos de una milésima de milímetro de "
"espesor en una dirección - una extrusión que falta, un archivo que falta, "
"una superficie donde se pretendía un sólido."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:391
msgid "``shell``: A body, not a skin"
msgstr "``shell``: Un cuerpo, no una piel"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:393
msgid "**Applies to** parts. ``pc test -f shell <object>`` runs it alone."
msgstr ""
"**Se aplica a** las piezas. ``pc test -f shell <object>`` la ejecuta sola."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:395
msgid ""
"Whether a part is a body rather than a skin: a set of faces with nothing "
"said about which side of them is material renders and exports like the part "
"that was meant, while every boolean against it comes back with no solid in "
"it - so interference, CAM, FEA and any mass computed from it are wrong. Read"
" straight out of the geometry the part has already produced, so it costs "
"nothing."
msgstr ""
"Si una pieza es un cuerpo y no una piel: un conjunto de caras sin nada dicho"
" sobre cuál de sus lados es material se renderiza y se exporta igual que la "
"pieza que se pretendía, mientras que toda operación booleana contra ella "
"vuelve sin ningún sólido dentro - así que la interferencia, el CAM, el FEA y"
" cualquier masa calculada a partir de ella están mal. Se lee directamente de"
" la geometría que la pieza ya ha producido, así que no cuesta nada."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:400
#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:438
msgid ""
"A sketch, which is not a body, and an assembly or a scene, which is checked "
"through its parts."
msgstr ""
"Un boceto, que no es un cuerpo, y un ensamblaje o una escena, que se "
"comprueban a través de sus piezas."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:405
msgid ""
"``The shape is a skin rather than a body: N shell(s) that no solid bounds "
"itself with``. A shell a script returns is closed into a solid "
"automatically, so either those faces enclose nothing - close them - or they "
"come from a file that states the part as a surface: export it from its tool "
"as a solid instead."
msgstr ""
"``The shape is a skin rather than a body: N shell(s) that no solid bounds "
"itself with``. Una cáscara que devuelve un script se cierra en un sólido "
"automáticamente, así que o esas caras no encierran nada - ciérrelas - o "
"vienen de un archivo que declara la pieza como superficie: expórtela de su "
"herramienta como sólido en su lugar."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:410
msgid "``solidity``: Not inside out"
msgstr "``solidity``: No está del revés"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:412
msgid "**Applies to** parts. ``pc test -f solidity <object>`` runs it alone."
msgstr ""
"**Se aplica a** las piezas. ``pc test -f solidity <object>`` la ejecuta "
"sola."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:414
msgid ""
"Whether every solid of a part has a positive volume. A solid whose faces are"
" oriented inward measures the right size and a negative volume: it renders "
"correctly, and every boolean against it is wrong. Asked before "
"``interference``, deliberately, since an inside-out part overlaps things it "
"is nowhere near."
msgstr ""
"Si todos los sólidos de una pieza tienen volumen positivo. Un sólido cuyas "
"caras están orientadas hacia dentro mide el tamaño correcto y un volumen "
"negativo: se renderiza correctamente, y toda operación booleana contra él "
"está mal. Se pregunta antes de ``interference``, deliberadamente, ya que una"
" pieza del revés se solapa con cosas de las que no está ni cerca."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:419
msgid ""
"A sketch, which has no solid, and an assembly or a scene, which is checked "
"through its parts."
msgstr ""
"Un boceto, que no tiene ningún sólido, y un ensamblaje o una escena, que se "
"comprueban a través de sus piezas."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:424
msgid ""
"``... a constituent solid measures ... mm^3``: negative means the faces are "
"oriented inward - fix their winding in the source (an LDraw part, for one, "
"has to state it); zero means the solid encloses nothing."
msgstr ""
"``... a constituent solid measures ... mm^3``: negativo significa que las "
"caras están orientadas hacia dentro - corrija su orientación en el origen "
"(una pieza de LDraw, por ejemplo, tiene que declararla); cero significa que "
"el sólido no encierra nada."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:429
msgid "``validity``: A well-formed solid"
msgstr "``validity``: Un sólido bien formado"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:431
msgid "**Applies to** parts. ``pc test -f validity <object>`` runs it alone."
msgstr ""
"**Se aplica a** las piezas. ``pc test -f validity <object>`` la ejecuta "
"sola."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:433
msgid ""
"Whether the geometry kernel certifies a part's solid as well formed. It "
"reports and never fails: the parts it has the most to say about are often "
"ones nothing is functionally wrong with. A part it reports on is one to "
"expect trouble from in anything exacting - booleans, meshing for print, CAM "
"- so treat a strange result from those as this rather than as the tool."
msgstr ""
"Si el núcleo geométrico certifica el sólido de una pieza como bien formado. "
"Informa y nunca falla: las piezas de las que más tiene que decir son a "
"menudo aquellas en las que nada está funcionalmente mal. Una pieza de la que"
" informa es una de la que esperar problemas en cualquier cosa exigente - "
"operaciones booleanas, mallado para impresión, CAM - así que interprete un "
"resultado extraño de esas cosas como esto y no como la herramienta."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:443
msgid ""
"It does not fail. When it says ``the geometry is a solid but not a well "
"formed one``, rebuild the part more simply where it can be - fewer tiny "
"faces, no self-intersections - or re-export it from its source."
msgstr ""
"No falla. Cuando dice ``the geometry is a solid but not a well formed one``,"
" reconstruya la pieza de forma más simple allí donde se pueda - menos caras "
"minúsculas, sin autointersecciones - o vuelva a exportarla desde su origen."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:448
msgid "``interference``: Parts do not overlap"
msgstr "``interference``: Las piezas no se solapan"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:450
msgid ""
"**Applies to** assemblies and scenes. ``pc test -f interference <object>`` "
"runs it alone."
msgstr ""
"**Se aplica a** ensamblajes y escenas. ``pc test -f interference <object>`` "
"la ejecuta sola."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:452
msgid ""
"Whether the parts of an assembly share space. Boxes are used only to pick "
"the pairs worth asking about; the answer comes from intersecting the two "
"solids and measuring what they share. Each sub-assembly declared in the "
"package answers for its own inside with its own verdict, so only what "
"crosses its boundary is looked at here. It is the most expensive of the "
"geometry checks."
msgstr ""
"Si las piezas de un ensamblaje comparten espacio. Las cajas se usan solo "
"para elegir los pares por los que vale la pena preguntar; la respuesta viene"
" de intersecar los dos sólidos y medir lo que comparten. Cada subensamblaje "
"declarado en el paquete responde por su propio interior con su propio "
"veredicto, así que aquí solo se mira lo que cruza su frontera. Es la más "
"costosa de las comprobaciones geométricas."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:454
msgid ""
"An overlap that is meant to be there is read from the joint between the two:"
" a port, an interface or a mating that says ``selfScrew`` (a screw cutting "
"its own thread, a nail making its own hole), a mating that says ``snapIn`` "
"(a pin pushed past a feature), a connection whose ``how:`` says either, and "
"a connection's ``interferes:``, naming the further items the same act of "
"joining drives through. Nothing is ever excused for a pair of parts by name."
msgstr ""
"Un solapamiento que debe estar ahí se lee de la unión entre los dos: un "
"puerto, una interfaz o un emparejamiento que dice ``selfScrew`` (un tornillo"
" que corta su propia rosca, un clavo que hace su propio agujero), un "
"emparejamiento que dice ``snapIn`` (un pasador empujado más allá de un "
"resalte), una conexión cuyo ``how:`` dice cualquiera de las dos cosas, y el "
"``interferes:`` de una conexión, que nombra los demás elementos que el mismo"
" acto de unión atraviesa. Nada se excusa nunca para un par de piezas "
"nombradas."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:464
msgid ""
"``'a' and 'b' share N mm^3``: the two are in each other. Each such failure "
"leaves an assembly to look at: the two parts where the assembly places them,"
" and a sub-assembly named ``interference`` holding what they share, one part"
" per volume. Open it from the IDE's Test tab, or with ``pc ide view`` and "
"its name (``<assembly>/interference/<a>+<b>``), and switch the two parts off"
" to see the overlap alone. Then move one of them - or, if the overlap is the"
" joint, say so on the joint."
msgstr ""
"``'a' and 'b' share N mm^3``: los dos están uno dentro del otro. Cada fallo "
"de este tipo deja un ensamblaje que mirar: las dos piezas donde las coloca "
"el ensamblaje, y un subensamblaje llamado ``interference`` con lo que "
"comparten, una pieza por volumen. Ábralo desde la pestaña Test del IDE, o "
"con ``pc ide view`` y su nombre (``<assembly>/interference/<a>+<b>``), y "
"apague las dos piezas para ver el solapamiento solo. Luego mueva una de "
"ellas - o, si el solapamiento es la unión, dígalo en la unión."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:465
msgid ""
"``'...' does not pass on its own``: a sub-assembly has overlaps of its own; "
"test it."
msgstr ""
"``'...' does not pass on its own``: un subensamblaje tiene solapamientos "
"propios; pruébelo."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:466
msgid ""
"``'...' names '...' in 'interferes:', which is not a link``: correct the "
"name; it is a link of the same ``links:`` list as the connection."
msgstr ""
"``'...' names '...' in 'interferes:', which is not a link``: corrija el "
"nombre; es un enlace de la misma lista ``links:`` que la conexión."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:467
msgid ""
"An object marked ``manufacturable: false`` (a scene, unless it says "
"otherwise) is told what overlaps rather than failed for it."
msgstr ""
"A un objeto marcado con ``manufacturable: false`` (una escena, a menos que "
"diga otra cosa) se le dice qué se solapa en lugar de darlo por fallado."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:472
msgid ""
"On the assembly: ``interference: minVolume:`` (in mm^3, default 0.05), below"
" which an overlap is taken for the arithmetic of two surfaces that touch, "
"and ``interference: minFraction:``, the same floor as a share of the smaller"
" part."
msgstr ""
"En el ensamblaje: ``interference: minVolume:`` (en mm^3, 0.05 por defecto), "
"por debajo del cual un solapamiento se toma por la aritmética de dos "
"superficies que se tocan, y ``interference: minFraction:``, el mismo umbral "
"como fracción de la pieza más pequeña."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:477
msgid "``cam``: A machine route can be produced"
msgstr "``cam``: Se puede producir una trayectoria de máquina"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:479
msgid ""
"**Applies to** parts and sketches that name a machine to be cut on. ``pc "
"test -f cam <object>`` runs it alone."
msgstr ""
"**Se aplica a** las piezas y los bocetos que nombran una máquina en la que "
"cortarse. ``pc test -f cam <object>`` la ejecuta sola."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:481
msgid ""
"Whether the program a machine cuts the object with can be produced: for "
"every ``cnc:``, ``laser:`` or ``drill:`` machine it names, the post-"
"processor that machine uses writes a route, and the route is thrown away. "
"The same code as ``pc cam``."
msgstr ""
"Si se puede producir el programa con el que una máquina corta el objeto: "
"para cada máquina ``cnc:``, ``laser:`` o ``drill:`` que nombra, el "
"posprocesador que usa esa máquina escribe una trayectoria, y la trayectoria "
"se descarta. El mismo código que ``pc cam``."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:486
msgid ""
"An object that names no machine to be routed on - nothing under "
"``manufacturing:`` asks for one, or only a ``cut:`` machine, which needs no "
"program."
msgstr ""
"Un objeto que no nombra ninguna máquina en la que trazar - nada bajo "
"``manufacturing:`` pide una, o solo una máquina ``cut:``, que no necesita "
"programa."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:491
msgid "A sentence about the section: a job key it cannot read; fix it."
msgstr ""
"Una frase sobre la sección: una clave de trabajo que no puede leer; "
"corríjala."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:492
msgid ""
"``the 'cam' implementation could not be resolved``: the implementation the "
"machine names is not a dependency of the package, or does not declare the "
"file type."
msgstr ""
"``the 'cam' implementation could not be resolved``: la implementación que "
"nombra la máquina no es una dependencia del paquete, o no declara el tipo de"
" archivo."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:493
msgid ""
"``no route was produced by ...``: the post-processor's error follows; fix "
"the tool or the outline it names, or run ``pc cam`` to see the whole report."
msgstr ""
"``no route was produced by ...``: a continuación va el error del "
"posprocesador; corrija la herramienta o el contorno que nombra, o ejecute "
"``pc cam`` para ver el informe completo."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:495
msgid ""
"It is skipped, with a warning, where the implementation cannot run on this "
"machine: start a container runtime, or install what it needs."
msgstr ""
"Se omite, con una advertencia, allí donde la implementación no puede "
"ejecutarse en esta máquina: arranque un runtime de contenedores, o instale "
"lo que necesita."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:500
msgid "``fea``: Structural analysis (FEA)"
msgstr "``fea``: Análisis estructural (FEA)"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:502
msgid ""
"**Applies to** parts that declare an ``fea:`` section. ``pc test -f fea "
"<object>`` runs it alone."
msgstr ""
"**Se aplica a** las piezas que declaran una sección ``fea:``. ``pc test -f "
"fea <object>`` la ejecuta sola."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:504
msgid ""
"Whether a part holds up under the loads each scenario of its ``fea:`` "
"section declares: every scenario is run by the implementation configured, "
"and the part passes when each of them ran and found nothing - the same "
"analyses as ``pc cae fea``, which runs one of them with ``-f <scenario>``."
msgstr ""
"Si una pieza resiste bajo las cargas que declara cada escenario de su "
"sección ``fea:``: cada escenario lo ejecuta la implementación configurada, y"
" la pieza pasa cuando todos ellos se ejecutaron y no encontraron nada - los "
"mismos análisis que ``pc cae fea``, que ejecuta uno de ellos con ``-f "
"<scenario>``."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:509
msgid "Anything but a part, and a part that declares no ``fea:`` section."
msgstr ""
"Cualquier cosa que no sea una pieza, y una pieza que no declara ninguna "
"sección ``fea:``."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:514
msgid ""
"A sentence about a scenario (``'fea: loaded:' declares neither 'fix:' nor "
"'load:'``, a key it does not take): fix the scenario it names."
msgstr ""
"Una frase sobre un escenario (``'fea: loaded:' declares neither 'fix:' nor "
"'load:'``, una clave que no acepta): corrija el escenario que nombra."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:515
msgid ""
"``FEA 'loaded' could not be run by ...``: the solver or the mesher is not "
"installed, or failed; the report says which. Install it, or name another "
"implementation."
msgstr ""
"``FEA 'loaded' could not be run by ...``: el solver o el mallador no está "
"instalado, o falló; el informe dice cuál. Instálelo, o nombre otra "
"implementación."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:516
msgid ""
"``FEA 'loaded' findings: ...``: the analysis ran and found a problem - a "
"stress, a deflection - at the place named. Change the design, or the load if"
" the load is what is wrong."
msgstr ""
"``FEA 'loaded' findings: ...``: el análisis se ejecutó y encontró un "
"problema - una tensión, una deflexión - en el lugar nombrado. Cambie el "
"diseño, o la carga si lo que está mal es la carga."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:518
#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:546
#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:574
#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:602
msgid ""
"It is skipped, with a warning, only where the implementation runs in a "
"container and there is no container runtime here."
msgstr ""
"Se omite, con una advertencia, solo allí donde la implementación se ejecuta "
"en un contenedor y aquí no hay ningún runtime de contenedores."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:523
msgid ""
"``fea: <scenario>: fix:``, ``load:`` (a force; a bare number is kilograms), "
"``gravity:``, ``implementation:`` and ``params:``; the user setting "
"``caeFeaImplementation``."
msgstr ""
"``fea: <scenario>: fix:``, ``load:`` (una fuerza; un número a secas son "
"kilogramos), ``gravity:``, ``implementation:`` y ``params:``; el ajuste de "
"usuario ``caeFeaImplementation``."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:528
msgid "``dynamic``: Vibration analysis (Dynamic FEA)"
msgstr "``dynamic``: Análisis de vibraciones (FEA dinámico)"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:530
msgid ""
"**Applies to** parts that declare a ``dynamic:`` section. ``pc test -f "
"dynamic <object>`` runs it alone."
msgstr ""
"**Se aplica a** las piezas que declaran una sección ``dynamic:``. ``pc test "
"-f dynamic <object>`` la ejecuta sola."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:532
msgid ""
"Whether a part, held as each scenario of its ``dynamic:`` section says, "
"rings only where it may: the modal analysis of every scenario is run by the "
"implementation configured, and the part passes when each ran and found "
"nothing - the same analyses as ``pc cae dynamic``. A natural frequency is a "
"property of the part and how it is held, not of what it carries, so a "
"scenario says only where it is held."
msgstr ""
"Si una pieza, sujeta como dice cada escenario de su sección ``dynamic:``, "
"solo vibra donde le está permitido: el análisis modal de cada escenario lo "
"ejecuta la implementación configurada, y la pieza pasa cuando todos se "
"ejecutaron y no encontraron nada - los mismos análisis que ``pc cae "
"dynamic``. Una frecuencia natural es una propiedad de la pieza y de cómo "
"está sujeta, no de lo que soporta, así que un escenario solo dice dónde está"
" sujeta."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:537
msgid "Anything but a part, and a part that declares no ``dynamic:`` section."
msgstr ""
"Cualquier cosa que no sea una pieza, y una pieza que no declara ninguna "
"sección ``dynamic:``."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:542
msgid ""
"A sentence about a scenario (``'dynamic: bolted:' declares none of 'fix:'``,"
" a key it does not take, such as ``load:``): fix the scenario it names."
msgstr ""
"Una frase sobre un escenario (``'dynamic: bolted:' declares none of "
"'fix:'``, una clave que no acepta, como ``load:``): corrija el escenario que"
" nombra."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:543
msgid ""
"``DYNAMIC 'bolted' could not be run by ...``: the solver or the mesher is "
"not installed, or failed; the report says which. Install it, or name another"
" implementation."
msgstr ""
"``DYNAMIC 'bolted' could not be run by ...``: el solver o el mallador no "
"está instalado, o falló; el informe dice cuál. Instálelo, o nombre otra "
"implementación."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:544
msgid ""
"``DYNAMIC 'bolted' findings: ...``: the analysis ran and found a problem - a"
" mode where the part must not ring. Change how it is held, or its stiffness "
"or mass."
msgstr ""
"``DYNAMIC 'bolted' findings: ...``: el análisis se ejecutó y encontró un "
"problema - un modo en el que la pieza no debe vibrar. Cambie cómo está "
"sujeta, o su rigidez o su masa."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:551
msgid ""
"``dynamic: <scenario>: fix:`` (the interfaces it is held by), "
"``implementation:`` and ``params:``; the user setting "
"``caeDynamicImplementation``."
msgstr ""
"``dynamic: <scenario>: fix:`` (las interfaces por las que está sujeta), "
"``implementation:`` y ``params:``; el ajuste de usuario "
"``caeDynamicImplementation``."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:556
msgid "``thermal``: Heat transfer"
msgstr "``thermal``: Transferencia de calor"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:558
msgid ""
"**Applies to** parts that declare a ``thermal:`` section. ``pc test -f "
"thermal <object>`` runs it alone."
msgstr ""
"**Se aplica a** las piezas que declaran una sección ``thermal:``. ``pc test "
"-f thermal <object>`` la ejecuta sola."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:560
msgid ""
"Whether a part, heated and cooled as each scenario of its ``thermal:`` "
"section says, stays as cool as it has to: every scenario is run by the "
"implementation configured, and the part passes when each ran and found "
"nothing - the same analyses as ``pc cae thermal``."
msgstr ""
"Si una pieza, calentada y enfriada como dice cada escenario de su sección "
"``thermal:``, se mantiene tan fría como tiene que mantenerse: cada escenario"
" lo ejecuta la implementación configurada, y la pieza pasa cuando todos se "
"ejecutaron y no encontraron nada - los mismos análisis que ``pc cae "
"thermal``."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:565
msgid "Anything but a part, and a part that declares no ``thermal:`` section."
msgstr ""
"Cualquier cosa que no sea una pieza, y una pieza que no declara ninguna "
"sección ``thermal:``."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:570
msgid ""
"A sentence about a scenario (``'thermal: in-use:' declares none of "
"'temperature:', 'heat:', 'convection:'``, a key it does not take): fix the "
"scenario it names."
msgstr ""
"Una frase sobre un escenario (``'thermal: in-use:' declares none of "
"'temperature:', 'heat:', 'convection:'``, una clave que no acepta): corrija "
"el escenario que nombra."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:571
msgid ""
"``THERMAL 'in-use' could not be run by ...``: the solver or the mesher is "
"not installed, or failed; the report says which. Install it, or name another"
" implementation."
msgstr ""
"``THERMAL 'in-use' could not be run by ...``: el solver o el mallador no "
"está instalado, o falló; el informe dice cuál. Instálelo, o nombre otra "
"implementación."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:572
msgid ""
"``THERMAL 'in-use' findings: ...``: the analysis ran and found a problem - a"
" temperature the part must not reach - at the place named. Change the "
"design, how it is cooled, or the heat if the heat is what is wrong."
msgstr ""
"``THERMAL 'in-use' findings: ...``: el análisis se ejecutó y encontró un "
"problema - una temperatura que la pieza no debe alcanzar - en el lugar "
"nombrado. Cambie el diseño, cómo se enfría, o el calor si lo que está mal es"
" el calor."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:579
msgid ""
"``thermal: <scenario>: temperature:`` (held at, in Celsius), ``heat:`` (put "
"in, in watts), ``convection:`` (a film coefficient, in W/(m^2\\*K)), "
"``implementation:`` and ``params:``; the user setting "
"``caeThermalImplementation``."
msgstr ""
"``thermal: <scenario>: temperature:`` (mantenida en, en grados Celsius), "
"``heat:`` (aportado, en vatios), ``convection:`` (un coeficiente de "
"película, en W/(m^2\\*K)), ``implementation:`` y ``params:``; el ajuste de "
"usuario ``caeThermalImplementation``."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:584
msgid "``cfd``: Flow analysis (CFD)"
msgstr "``cfd``: Análisis de flujo (CFD)"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:586
msgid ""
"**Applies to** parts that declare a ``cfd:`` section. ``pc test -f cfd "
"<object>`` runs it alone."
msgstr ""
"**Se aplica a** las piezas que declaran una sección ``cfd:``. ``pc test -f "
"cfd <object>`` la ejecuta sola."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:588
msgid ""
"Whether a part behaves in the flow each scenario of its ``cfd:`` section "
"declares: every scenario is run by the implementation configured, and the "
"part passes when each ran and found nothing - the same analyses as ``pc cae "
"cfd``."
msgstr ""
"Si una pieza se comporta en el flujo que declara cada escenario de su "
"sección ``cfd:``: cada escenario lo ejecuta la implementación configurada, y"
" la pieza pasa cuando todos se ejecutaron y no encontraron nada - los mismos"
" análisis que ``pc cae cfd``."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:593
msgid "Anything but a part, and a part that declares no ``cfd:`` section."
msgstr ""
"Cualquier cosa que no sea una pieza, y una pieza que no declara ninguna "
"sección ``cfd:``."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:598
msgid "A sentence about a scenario: fix the scenario it names."
msgstr "Una frase sobre un escenario: corrija el escenario que nombra."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:599
msgid ""
"``CFD '<scenario>' could not be run by ...``: the solver is not installed, "
"or failed; the report says which."
msgstr ""
"``CFD '<scenario>' could not be run by ...``: el solver no está instalado, o"
" falló; el informe dice cuál."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:600
msgid ""
"``CFD '<scenario>' findings: ...``: the analysis ran and found a problem at "
"the place named."
msgstr ""
"``CFD '<scenario>' findings: ...``: el análisis se ejecutó y encontró un "
"problema en el lugar nombrado."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:607
msgid ""
"``cfd: <scenario>: fix:``, ``load:``, ``outlet:``, ``implementation:`` and "
"``params:``; the user setting ``caeCfdImplementation``."
msgstr ""
"``cfd: <scenario>: fix:``, ``load:``, ``outlet:``, ``implementation:`` y "
"``params:``; el ajuste de usuario ``caeCfdImplementation``."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:612
msgid "``sim``: Does what its simulations say"
msgstr "``sim``: Hace lo que dicen sus simulaciones"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:614
msgid ""
"**Applies to** parts, assemblies and scenes that declare ``simulate:``. ``pc"
" test -f sim <object>`` runs it alone."
msgstr ""
"**Se aplica a** las piezas, los ensamblajes y las escenas que declaran "
"``simulate:``. ``pc test -f sim <object>`` la ejecuta sola."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:616
msgid ""
"Whether the object does what its ``simulate:`` section says it does: each "
"simulation is run - the object placed in its scene and handed to the "
"simulation plugin - and its ``validation:`` condition has to hold over what "
"came back. The same runs as ``pc sim``, which also prints everything the "
"plugin reported (``--json``). It is the most expensive question ``pc test`` "
"asks, and is asked last."
msgstr ""
"Si el objeto hace lo que su sección ``simulate:`` dice que hace: cada "
"simulación se ejecuta - el objeto se coloca en su escena y se entrega al "
"plugin de simulación - y su condición ``validation:`` tiene que cumplirse "
"sobre lo que volvió. Las mismas ejecuciones que ``pc sim``, que además "
"imprime todo lo que informó el plugin (``--json``). Es la pregunta más "
"costosa que plantea ``pc test``, y se plantea la última."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:621
msgid ""
"Anything but a part, an assembly or a scene, and one that declares no "
"simulation."
msgstr ""
"Cualquier cosa que no sea una pieza, un ensamblaje o una escena, y una que "
"no declara ninguna simulación."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:626
msgid ""
"``... ran, and its 'validation' does not hold``: the object did not behave "
"as claimed. Run ``pc sim --json`` to see ``before`` and ``after``, then "
"change the design, or the condition if the condition is what is wrong."
msgstr ""
"``... ran, and its 'validation' does not hold``: el objeto no se comportó "
"como se afirmaba. Ejecute ``pc sim --json`` para ver ``before`` y ``after``,"
" y luego cambie el diseño, o la condición si lo que está mal es la "
"condición."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:627
msgid ""
"``... could not be run``: the plugin or the scene the entry names is not "
"found, or the simulator failed; the report says which."
msgstr ""
"``... could not be run``: el plugin o la escena que nombra la entrada no se "
"encuentra, o el simulador falló; el informe dice cuál."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:628
msgid ""
"``... states no 'validation'``: asked about by name, an entry with no "
"condition fails; add one over ``before`` and ``after``. Walked to as part of"
" a package, it is skipped instead."
msgstr ""
"``... states no 'validation'``: preguntada por su nombre, una entrada sin "
"condición falla; añada una sobre ``before`` y ``after``. Si se llega a ella "
"como parte de un paquete, se omite en su lugar."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:630
msgid ""
"It is skipped, with a warning, where the simulator runs in a container and "
"there is no container runtime here."
msgstr ""
"Se omite, con una advertencia, allí donde el simulador se ejecuta en un "
"contenedor y aquí no hay ningún runtime de contenedores."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:635
msgid ""
"``simulate: <name>:`` - ``simulation:`` (the plugin), ``scene:``, "
"``validation:``, and ``feature:``, the feature of the requirements it "
"demonstrates."
msgstr ""
"``simulate: <name>:`` - ``simulation:`` (el plugin), ``scene:``, "
"``validation:``, y ``feature:``, la característica de los requisitos que "
"demuestra."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:640
msgid "Agent skills"
msgstr "Skills de agente"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:642
msgid "``/pc:validate``"
msgstr "``/pc:validate``"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:643
msgid ""
"Runs ``pc test`` as the first thing it does, and then goes beyond it: it "
"runs every simulation and every analysis scenario, renders the object from "
"every angle that matters with its ports and interfaces drawn, reads the bill"
" of materials and the assembly instructions of an assembly, and gives every "
"requirement a verdict -- met, not met, or \"cannot tell\" -- with the "
"evidence named. The ``features:`` half of a requirement is prose, which no "
"check here can measure, and it is judged there and nowhere else."
msgstr ""
"Ejecuta ``pc test`` como primera cosa que hace, y luego va más allá: ejecuta"
" todas las simulaciones y todos los escenarios de análisis, renderiza el "
"objeto desde todos los ángulos que importan con sus puertos e interfaces "
"dibujados, lee la lista de materiales y las instrucciones de montaje de un "
"ensamblaje, y da a cada requisito un veredicto -- cumplido, no cumplido, o "
"\"no se puede saber\" -- con la evidencia nombrada. La mitad ``features:`` "
"de un requisito es prosa, que ninguna comprobación de aquí puede medir, y se"
" juzga allí y en ningún otro sitio."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:651
msgid "``/pc:sim-assembly-fea``"
msgstr "``/pc:sim-assembly-fea``"

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:652
msgid ""
"Produces the ``fea:`` scenario that the ``fea`` check below then holds the "
"part to, out of what a simulation of its assembly measured."
msgstr ""
"Produce el escenario ``fea:`` al que la comprobación ``fea`` de más abajo "
"somete luego la pieza, a partir de lo que midió una simulación de su "
"ensamblaje."

#: ../../source/digital_thread/lifecycle/testing.rst:655
msgid ""
"Every skill runs these same commands, through the same cache, so a verdict "
"an agent reports is a verdict you can reproduce by hand."
msgstr ""
"Todas las skills ejecutan estos mismos comandos, a través de la misma caché,"
" así que un veredicto del que informa un agente es un veredicto que usted "
"puede reproducir a mano."
